<title>CANADA: Canada dollar firmer on Thiessen remarks, U.S data.</title>
<headline>Canada dollar firmer on Thiessen remarks, U.S data.</headline>
<text>
<p>FORECAST RANGE   1.3775/1.3850	    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3894</p>
<p>RESISTANCE 1.3790   SUPPORT 1.3920	HI 1.3901   LO  1.3852</p>
<p>CANADA OPEN  1.3846/51    HI 1.3870     EUROPE OPEN     1.3850</p>
<p>PREV CLOSE   1.3893/98    LO 1.3827     HI 1.3886   LO  1.3876</p>
<p>---------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* Canada's dollar strengthened to C$1.3790 (US$0.7251) on Thursday in midday trading as investors reacted to positive comments by Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen and signs of waning U.S. inflation, traders said. * They said the rally prompted the Bank of Canada to intervene and sell Canadian dollars for U.S. near the C$1.3828 (US$0.7231) level.</p>
